{"cases":[{"attack":true,"case":"The claim suggests that shifting the problem into p-adic integers provides a resolution via a 'contracting operator,' but fails to acknowledge that the 3n+1 map is not a contraction on Z_2; in fact, it is a measure-preserving isometry on the 2-adic integers, meaning it does not naturally 'contract' trajectories toward 1.","target":"4949a383b954299f398bccb40515d0b286abc4a74e4af98f357bfcf16e42199d"},{"attack":true,"case":"The claim asserts the conjecture is 'likely false' due to the existence of a non-trivial cycle, yet presents this as a fact ('there exists a counterexample') without providing a value or proof, effectively inventing a counterexample that has not been discovered in mathematical literature.","target":"8bd12a60cf9eba3f8ac2ce62ea73890104e0cfb4f98f9600e6094ce622e7e2e4"},{"attack":true,"case":"The claim asserts the conjecture is 'formally undecidable within ZFC' as a definitive state of the problem, whereas undecidability is itself an unsettled hypothesis and not a proven property of the Collatz conjecture.","target":"cd36bf34d053d0b2e9958008575854e54d4f292714d84ed179160239545550ee"}]}